            <div xml:id="d61">

                <pb facs="0160" n="61" sameAs="frus:frus1936v05/pg61"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.34119/571: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chargé in Argentina</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Cox</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-08-31T17:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1936—5
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>115. For Braden. Your despatch 240, August 21. Major Weeks authorized to act as
                    observer. Submit estimate in accordance with the Department’s instruction 417,
                    July 17, 1936,<anchor n="44" xml:id="d61-f1"/> and inform Department if
                    necessary drafts will be drawn at Santiago or Buenos Aires.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
